    "frd_landing_faqs_T6CfUG": {
      "type": "frd-landing-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "content_kgNa3D": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are the benefits of upgrading to a gas insert?",
            "answer": "<p>Gas inserts provide higher heat efficiency, lower heating costs, and cleaner indoor air. They’re easier to operate with just the push of a button and require minimal maintenance. Plus, their sleek designs and cozy flames make them both practical and stylish.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_PiATVf": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What should I expect during the consultation and installation process?",
            "answer": "<p>We take care of everything.We’ll send our friendly pros to your place. They’ll measure and confirm options with you, providing a more accurate and detailed project estimate and timeline. Then a licensed contractor will run a gas line and electric as needed. Our pros will install your gas insert in less than a day (typically). No drywall dust, major construction.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_frgVt8": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are gas inserts safe to use around kids and pets?",
            "answer": "<p>Gas fireplace inserts are a safe solution when installed properly. Because gas inserts are a sealed system, there is zero direct contact with an open flame .</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_hKc48K": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is a gas fireplace insert worth it?",
            "answer": "<p>The average cost of a Heat & Glo insert, plus installation, is around $6,500 but will vary depending on your home. Compared to other home renovation projects, an insert is less expensive and is ready to use and enjoy, faster. Plus, a gas fireplace can increase a home’s value up to 12 percent.</p>"
          }
        },
        "content_j3PEVX": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What if I don't currently have a fireplace?",
            "answer": "<p>We have all kinds of fireplace solutions. While an insert only accommodates an existing, wood-burning fireplace, we offer gas, wood and electric fireplaces that can be installed at any time. The installation and construction process will be different depending on what fireplace you choose.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
